✅ Day 1: Introduction & File Management (Basics)

🎯 Goals:

Understand what Linux is.

Learn basic file and directory management commands.

🧠 1. What is Linux?

Linux is an open-source operating system.

It's used in servers, desktops, mobile devices, and cloud infrastructure.

The most common shell in Linux is Bash (Bourne Again SHell).

💻 2. Basic Linux Commands (File & Directory Management)


 Command                	Description

pwd	                    Print current directory
ls	                    List files in the current directory
cd	                    Change directory
mkdir	                    Create a new directory
touch	                    Create a new empty file
cp	                    Copy files or directories
mv	                    Move or rename files
rm	                    Delete files
rmdir	                    Remove empty directory
cat	                    Display content of a file
clear	                    Clear terminal screen
 

🔧 3. Practical Tasks


✅ Task 1: Check your current location

pwd

✅ Task 2: Create a directory called practice

mkdir practice
cd practice

✅ Task 3: Create 3 files

touch file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt
ls

✅ Task 4: Rename file1.txt to renamed.txt

mv file1.txt renamed.txt

✅ Task 5: Copy renamed.txt to a new file called copy.txt

cp renamed.txt copy.txt

✅ Task 6: Delete file2.txt

rm file2.txt

✅ Task 7: Display the contents of a file

echo "Hello Linux!" > hello.txt
cat hello.txt
